    ]
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Valmont buys horses with their eventual resale in mind. Anthony Ramsden and his bloodstock agent seek value among yearlings expected to mature later, accepting that some will need to progress through handicap races. Training decisions and sales are parts of the same commercial plan, with new horses following those that leave.\n\nJoint purchases bring another layer of selection. When Ramsden partnered with Michael Blencowe, their respective agents compared auction shortlists, agreed which horses suited both owners and set a bidding limit. The arrangement placed horses with several trainers, while allowing either owner to pursue a purchase separately when their preferences differed.",
    "html": "<p>Valmont buys horses with their eventual resale in mind. Anthony Ramsden and his bloodstock agent seek value among yearlings expected to mature later, accepting that some will need to progress through handicap races. Training decisions and sales are parts of the same commercial plan, with new horses following those that leave.</p>\r\n<p>Joint purchases bring another layer of selection. When Ramsden partnered with Michael Blencowe, their respective agents compared auction shortlists, agreed which horses suited both owners and set a bidding limit. The arrangement placed horses with several trainers, while allowing either owner to pursue a purchase separately when their preferences differed.</p>\r\n",
    "word_count": 101,
